{% endmacro %}
{# W3C SCXML 6.2.5: the act a send to a processor the host serves performs, for `processor_type`.
   One body for the two ways a send reaches it: a type the build saw served by the host
   (`send_type_host_served`, a Mesh send the build lowered among them) and a `targetexpr` that
   names a Mesh peer once it is evaluated (SCE_MESH.md §mesh-19). The whole send is the host's,
   handed the request the document wrote, so the arm is the only delivery the element makes:
   delivering the event locally as well would show the document the act twice. Its target is
   passed through uninterpreted, a delay is a property of the send and not of the processor, and
   the request is the one of this moment, its `_event.invokeid` included (SCE_MESH.md §10.7).
   `value` is the message a test component's send carries as a value, and none for every other
   send. #}
{% macro host_send_arm(processor_type, event_name, target, content, params, send_id, delay, value) %}
                    // W3C SCXML 6.2.5: "{{ processor_type }}" is served by the host, which declared it to this
                    // build. The send is dispatched and not refused, and the whole of it is the
                    // host's: delivering the event locally as well would show the document the act
                    // twice.
                    let sendRequest = HostSendRequest(
                        processorType: "{{ processor_type | escape_swift }}",
                        eventName: {{ event_name }},
                        target: {{ target }},
                        content: {{ content }},
                        params: {{ params }},
                        sendID: {{ send_id }},
                        eventData: sendEventData,
{% if value %}
                        invokeID: engine.currentEventInvokeID,
{# docs/SCE_TEST_PROFILE.md §12.3: a test component's message is the value of
   its specific template, handed to the test-port processor as a value and
   never as an encoding (docs/adr/0091, C2), with the writer of its canonical
   form in the test log (§12.5). Every other send leaves it nil and carries
   `eventData`. #}
                        value: HostSendValue({{ value }})
{% else %}
                        invokeID: engine.currentEventInvokeID
{% endif %}
                    )
{% if delay %}
                    engine.scheduleHostSend(delay: {{ delay }}, request: sendRequest, sender: self.sessionID)
{% else %}
                    engine.performHostSend(sendRequest)
{% endif %}
